WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.704 --> 00:00:39.508
The year is 1582.

2
00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:44.179
Nobunaga Oda, who sought to
unify Japan, is murdered by

3
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.384
his own general, Mitsuhide Akechi,
before his dream is realized.

4
00:00:48.385 --> 00:00:52.187
However, Hideyoshi Toyotomi,
Nobunaga's right-hand man,

5
00:00:52.188 --> 00:00:54.156
defeats Mitsuhide.

6
00:00:54.157 --> 00:00:59.161
Toyotomi's reign as Nobunaga's
successor is solidified.

7
00:00:59.162 --> 00:01:01.831
The embers of conflict
continue to burn,

8
00:01:01.832 --> 00:01:05.598
but the country is visited
by a temporary peace.

9
00:02:23.751 --> 00:02:25.082
Stupid bastards!

10
00:02:57.887 --> 00:02:59.946
Open the gates!

11
00:03:10.399 --> 00:03:12.701
You are Bunzaemon Kinokuniya?

12
00:03:12.702 --> 00:03:14.135
Yes.

13
00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:20.576
By order of Lord Hideyoshi, we
have come to confiscate any items

14
00:03:20.577 --> 00:03:23.740
left behind by the traitor
Mitsuhide Akechi.

15
00:03:25.582 --> 00:03:27.846
Hand them over now!

16
00:03:32.556 --> 00:03:36.193
I'm telling you, I have no
recollection of having met Akechi

17
00:03:36.194 --> 00:03:39.891
nor of receiving
anything of his!

18
00:03:53.778 --> 00:03:55.345
Check the storehouse.

19
00:03:55.346 --> 00:03:58.077
We shall decide whether
any items are here.

20
00:04:24.377 --> 00:04:24.943
"Go"

21
00:04:24.944 --> 00:04:25.477
"Go" Thief! It's a thief!

22
00:04:25.478 --> 00:04:28.614
Thief! It's a thief!

23
00:04:28.615 --> 00:04:29.715
"Go" Thief! It's a thief!

24
00:04:29.716 --> 00:04:30.045
Thief! It's a thief!

25
00:04:32.552 --> 00:04:34.086
So...

26
00:04:34.087 --> 00:04:37.921
This is here? Or this is here?

27
00:04:50.404 --> 00:04:55.307
Then go through here, and
that leads out to...

28
00:04:56.677 --> 00:04:58.144
Huh?

29
00:04:58.145 --> 00:05:01.638
There he is! Get him!

30
00:05:05.453 --> 00:05:09.583
Sasuke, you idiot. This is so
not what you said it would be!

31
00:05:42.858 --> 00:05:44.553
Yeah, right.

32
00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.973
You try and steal from a
public official like me?

33
00:05:56.974 --> 00:06:00.034
That's not good.

34
00:06:01.979 --> 00:06:03.879
Ah! It's Goemon!

35
00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.081
Huh? Where?!

36
00:06:05.082 --> 00:06:07.551
Oh! There!

37
00:06:13.992 --> 00:06:15.726
Goemon!

38
00:06:15.727 --> 00:06:19.930
Whoa. Now that's a sight!

39
00:06:19.931 --> 00:06:20.764
That's!

40
00:06:20.765 --> 00:06:24.735
Yeah. The greatest thief in the
world, and friend to the poor,

41
00:06:24.736 --> 00:06:28.365
Goemon Ishikawa.
He's so awesome!

42
00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.183
Hey!

43
00:06:39.184 --> 00:06:41.675
Go! It's Goemon!

44
00:06:45.557 --> 00:06:48.390
The heck? It's empty.

45
00:07:01.107 --> 00:07:04.565
Do it up tonight!

46
00:07:15.723 --> 00:07:18.491
Bastard! Get down from there!
You're under arrest!

47
00:07:18.492 --> 00:07:22.826
Of course I ain't gettin'
down from here. Dumbass!

48
00:07:31.305 --> 00:07:34.104
Later, guys.

49
00:07:39.281 --> 00:07:43.581
Goemon! You're the
best in all Japan!

50
00:08:13.883 --> 00:08:15.282
Say, Mr. Ishikawa...

51
00:08:15.283 --> 00:08:16.784
Hm?

52
00:08:16.785 --> 00:08:20.522
Will you finally take
one of them tonight?

53
00:08:20.523 --> 00:08:24.826
Huh? I guess, but...
I got no money!

54
00:08:24.827 --> 00:08:32.968
That's of no concern. I will
pay all your bills here.

55
00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:35.203
That's a lovely thing.

56
00:08:35.204 --> 00:08:37.502
Goemon!

57
00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:45.515
I missed you so much! Say, Goemon,
tonight will be my turn, right?

58
00:08:45.516 --> 00:08:48.317
You don't care for these
pissant little girls, do you?

59
00:08:48.318 --> 00:08:52.021
Huh? I would be a far better
choice than you, of course.

60
00:08:52.022 --> 00:08:55.423
Well, I'd take either of ya.

61
00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:04.495
What are you looking at?

62
00:09:07.438 --> 00:09:11.397
Okay! Shall we dance?!

63
00:09:18.116 --> 00:09:21.950
It's not here. It must
have been that thief.

64
00:09:25.724 --> 00:09:28.090
"Go"

65
00:09:31.363 --> 00:09:32.694
Saizo.

66
00:09:39.738 --> 00:09:41.906
Just who is he?

67
00:09:41.907 --> 00:09:45.477
A thief who's been making a name
for himself around town recently.

68
00:09:45.478 --> 00:09:49.915
He has the box. You must
get it back from him.

69
00:09:49.916 --> 00:09:50.616
Sir.

70
00:09:50.617 --> 00:09:52.585
Also...

71
00:09:52.586 --> 00:09:58.958
Kill everyone in this house.
I'm sure you understand.

72
00:09:58.959 --> 00:10:02.394
Women, children... Everyone.

73
00:10:02.395 --> 00:10:05.664
I will visit Lord
Hideyoshi tomorrow.

74
00:10:05.665 --> 00:10:10.899
He must know nothing of the box.
Understand?

75
00:12:27.114 --> 00:12:29.148
Sasuke.

76
00:12:29.149 --> 00:12:30.916
Washcloth.

77
00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:33.552
Huh? How'd you know I was here?

78
00:12:33.553 --> 00:12:37.123
It was obvious. Just hurry
up and give me one.

79
00:12:37.124 --> 00:12:42.095
Okay, okay. You sure are
a slave driver. Here.

80
00:12:42.096 --> 00:12:43.256
Gotcha.

81
00:12:43.965 --> 00:12:48.502
Ow! Just what are
you doing, sir?!

82
00:12:48.503 --> 00:12:50.337
It's obvious, fool.

83
00:12:50.338 --> 00:12:51.571
What is?

84
00:12:51.572 --> 00:12:57.911
Don't "What is?" me. This map.
It's completely wrong!

85
00:12:57.912 --> 00:13:00.847
That caused me a lot
of trouble yesterday!

86
00:13:00.848 --> 00:13:03.784
Huh? Oh, really?

87
00:13:05.354 --> 00:13:08.356
There's yesterday's take.

88
00:13:08.357 --> 00:13:10.825
Thank you, as always!

89
00:13:10.826 --> 00:13:15.463
By the way, you're not still
gunning for me, are you?

90
00:13:15.464 --> 00:13:20.101
Perish the thought! I thought you
were just a masterless samurai.

91
00:13:20.102 --> 00:13:24.807
You beat me time and again.
Also...

92
00:13:24.808 --> 00:13:29.111
I make so much money
being your ally!

93
00:13:29.112 --> 00:13:30.846
That you do.

94
00:13:30.847 --> 00:13:36.685
By the by, it seems last night's
mansion was no ordinary mansion.

95
00:13:36.686 --> 00:13:38.687
Mitsunari Ishida of the
Five Commissioners

96
00:13:38.688 --> 00:13:44.460
has apparently gone and seized it.
Something about a lacquered box...

97
00:13:44.461 --> 00:13:51.234
It wasn't there, so they've been
raising hell in town looking for it.

98
00:13:51.235 --> 00:13:55.371
So this lacquered box...
was it this big?

99
00:13:55.372 --> 00:13:56.239
Probably.

100
00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.140
And blue?

101
00:13:57.141 --> 00:13:58.808
Uh-oh.

102
00:13:58.809 --> 00:14:00.043
Yeah, I snatched it.

103
00:14:00.044 --> 00:14:00.710
I knew it!

104
00:14:00.711 --> 00:14:02.745
Why didn't you
tell me about it?!

105
00:14:02.746 --> 00:14:08.752
I didn't know it was there either!
So, where is it?

106
00:14:08.753 --> 00:14:10.421
I tossed it.

107
00:14:10.422 --> 00:14:12.590
Thank goodness!

108
00:14:12.591 --> 00:14:17.695
Every family member and servant
in that mansion was slaughtered!

109
00:14:17.696 --> 00:14:20.164
It's just terrible.

110
00:14:22.067 --> 00:14:24.535
Seems kinda interesting.

111
00:14:24.536 --> 00:14:25.936
Huh?

112
00:14:25.937 --> 00:14:28.839
I'm going. I'm gonna
look for that box.

113
00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:33.778
Sir, that's a bad idea! Mitsunari
has put Saizo on the job!

114
00:14:34.881 --> 00:14:37.716
The Saizo Kirigakure...

115
00:14:37.717 --> 00:14:40.685
I ain't never heard of him.

116
00:14:40.686 --> 00:14:43.121
In underworld circles, he's
the most infamous of shinobi.

117
00:14:43.122 --> 00:14:49.761
They say he's fiercely talented. So,
let's not get too involved. Okay?

118
00:14:49.762 --> 00:14:51.355
I'm going.

119
00:15:14.389 --> 00:15:16.657
Well?

120
00:15:16.658 --> 00:15:23.664
This box is from the Christian,
and it can play music.

121
00:15:23.665 --> 00:15:30.434
Those buggers make one
interesting thing after another.

122
00:15:32.307 --> 00:15:34.942
Mitsunari.

123
00:15:34.943 --> 00:15:39.681
You seem busy lately.

124
00:15:39.682 --> 00:15:44.915
Sir. All on your behalf, Lord.

125
00:15:49.091 --> 00:15:52.327
On my behalf, huh?

126
00:15:52.328 --> 00:15:57.499
Mitsunari... Just what're
you looking for?

127
00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:01.937
Your meaning, sir?

128
00:16:01.938 --> 00:16:04.273
Don't screw with me!

129
00:16:04.274 --> 00:16:09.473
A box, isn't it?
A lacquered one.

130
00:16:13.717 --> 00:16:20.690
Oh yes, Mr. Ishikawa. That
gentleman left this morning.

131
00:16:20.691 --> 00:16:22.559
Is that so?

132
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.996
Say, Yashichi, I'm thirsty.
Bring me some water.

133
00:16:25.997 --> 00:16:31.001
Yes, ma'am. Right... Huh?

134
00:16:31.002 --> 00:16:32.702
An example?

135
00:16:32.703 --> 00:16:36.072
Sir. The selling of any
lacquered goods is banned.

136
00:16:36.073 --> 00:16:39.909
I believed your influence would
be weakened if we did nothing.

137
00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:46.183
I saw to this matter myself. I
apologize for acting out of turn.

138
00:16:46.184 --> 00:16:48.219
You are one of the
Five Commissioners,

139
00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:53.891
appointed personally by me.
Do not act "out of turn."

140
00:16:53.892 --> 00:16:57.521
If you go too far...

141
00:17:03.269 --> 00:17:06.004
My lord! Lady
Chacha has arrived!

142
00:17:06.005 --> 00:17:08.872
Ah! She's here, eh?

143
00:17:15.882 --> 00:17:20.615
How fortunate for
you, Lord Ishida.

144
00:17:24.625 --> 00:17:32.098
Lord Tokugawa. What do
you mean, "fortunate"?

145
00:17:32.099 --> 00:17:37.537
I glimpsed Lady Chacha earlier.

146
00:17:37.538 --> 00:17:43.710
Long had it been since I'd seen her.
She grows more and more beautiful.

147
00:17:43.711 --> 00:17:50.250
One can see how Lord Hideyoshi
would become entranced.

148
00:17:50.251 --> 00:17:55.322
Lady Chacha is the niece
of Lord Nobunaga.

149
00:17:55.323 --> 00:17:58.959
Lord Hideyoshi was his
most trusted retainer.

150
00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:02.396
No doubt she is as
if his daughter.

151
00:18:02.397 --> 00:18:05.132
However...

152
00:18:05.133 --> 00:18:09.400
Is that all, I wonder?

153
00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.801
Farewell.

154
00:18:15.311 --> 00:18:17.112
Chacha...

155
00:18:17.113 --> 00:18:21.683
Following Lord Nobunaga's death,
I have acted as your father

156
00:18:21.684 --> 00:18:26.187
for how many years now is it?

157
00:18:26.188 --> 00:18:30.459
It has been 15 years since then.

158
00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.495
What could I possibly
say to thank you?

159
00:18:32.496 --> 00:18:38.267
What are you saying? I've
simply acted as I should...

160
00:18:38.268 --> 00:18:46.875
If not for Lord Nobunaga, I would
have died still a poor farmer.

161
00:18:46.876 --> 00:18:56.619
But now I am the great
Hideyoshi, the supreme ruler!

162
00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.647
The ways of the world change...

163
00:19:02.826 --> 00:19:07.854
Chacha, you must change, too.

164
00:19:12.002 --> 00:19:14.638
Become my concubine.

165
00:19:14.639 --> 00:19:20.410
Will you be my concubine
and bear me a child?

166
00:19:20.411 --> 00:19:25.576
A child to continue the
Nobunaga bloodline...

167
00:19:28.319 --> 00:19:29.519
Who is it?

168
00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.989
I, Rikkyu.

169
00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:38.596
Oh, my! Lord Hideyoshi!
I shall return later.

170
00:19:38.597 --> 00:19:42.556
No. I was about to leave.

171
00:19:45.237 --> 00:19:46.270
Rikkyu.

172
00:19:46.271 --> 00:19:46.938
Sir.

173
00:19:46.939 --> 00:19:51.609
Chacha will remain here in the
castle for the time being.

174
00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:56.070
I await a favorable reply.

175
00:20:05.091 --> 00:20:09.461
Such a long time it has
been, Lady Chacha!

176
00:20:09.462 --> 00:20:13.098
You must be tired after
your long journey.

177
00:20:13.099 --> 00:20:18.871
Ah, yes! I shall
bring you some tea.

178
00:20:18.872 --> 00:20:20.306
Rikkyu...

179
00:20:20.307 --> 00:20:21.604
My lady?

180
00:20:23.644 --> 00:20:26.212
In this land...

181
00:20:26.213 --> 00:20:30.775
Can one see fireflies
in this land?

182
00:20:34.088 --> 00:20:36.989
Come on, please wait, sir!

183
00:20:38.225 --> 00:20:42.229
How are you going to look for
it in the midst of all this?

184
00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.732
Instinct, I guess.

185
00:20:44.733 --> 00:20:47.463
I thought it'd be
something like that.

186
00:20:49.404 --> 00:20:51.804
C'mon, Mom. Eat.

187
00:20:53.808 --> 00:20:55.242
Koheita, this...

188
00:20:55.243 --> 00:21:01.182
What, you think I stole it?
I saw Goemon yesterday!

189
00:21:02.517 --> 00:21:03.485
What about you?

190
00:21:03.486 --> 00:21:09.357
I ate earlier, so I'm okay.
C'mon, eat.

191
00:21:09.358 --> 00:21:11.485
Thank you.

192
00:21:20.369 --> 00:21:22.860
It's delicious.

193
00:21:27.978 --> 00:21:33.382
Mom! Are you all right? Hold on.
I'll buy you some medicine.

194
00:21:40.891 --> 00:21:42.858
Hey.

195
00:21:42.859 --> 00:21:48.465
It stinks! This is where
the absolute poorest live.

196
00:21:48.466 --> 00:21:52.069
Since they opened
up the free market,

197
00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:55.072
it's well and good for
those who make it...

198
00:21:55.073 --> 00:21:59.509
but this is what happens
to all the weak ones.

199
00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:03.747
It's brought riches, but
it's brought disparity, too.

200
00:22:03.748 --> 00:22:07.417
"The strong devour
the weak," huh?

201
00:22:07.418 --> 00:22:14.689
Whether that's good or not...
Right, sir?

202
00:22:15.494 --> 00:22:18.563
There you go. There, there.

203
00:22:18.564 --> 00:22:20.264
You don't plan on
searching, do you?

204
00:22:20.265 --> 00:22:22.893
That ain't it at all.

205
00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:25.837
Mom!

206
00:22:25.838 --> 00:22:26.938
- Is this all right?
- Mom!

207
00:22:26.939 --> 00:22:28.773
- It's fine.
- Mom!

208
00:22:28.774 --> 00:22:32.040
Scum like this are
a dime a dozen.

209
00:22:43.456 --> 00:22:45.224
Who are you, bastard?

210
00:22:45.225 --> 00:22:47.893
If you don't want your prized sword
cutting of that head of yours,

211
00:22:47.894 --> 00:22:50.226
then get the hell out of here.

212
00:22:59.573 --> 00:23:01.632
Bro!

213
00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:04.744
Sir!

214
00:23:04.745 --> 00:23:06.610
Hurry!

215
00:23:08.949 --> 00:23:13.653
Sir, that was going too far!

216
00:23:13.654 --> 00:23:21.562
Mom... Mom! Why? Why?

217
00:23:22.764 --> 00:23:25.255
Because you're weak.

218
00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:32.807
You thought that, didn't you? You can't win.
You'll be killed.

219
00:23:32.808 --> 00:23:36.973
That this wouldn't have happened
if you were stronger than them.

220
00:23:38.648 --> 00:23:41.450
Am I wrong?

221
00:23:41.451 --> 00:23:48.687
Become stronger, boy. Then
nothing can be taken from you.

222
00:23:52.128 --> 00:23:54.763
I'm borrowing this box.

223
00:23:54.764 --> 00:23:59.001
Okay! We've got the box, so
let's get out of here, sir!

224
00:23:59.002 --> 00:24:02.028
It's too late.

225
00:24:05.175 --> 00:24:06.509
What's with him?

226
00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:08.845
It's Saizo.

227
00:24:08.846 --> 00:24:11.214
Huh? Huh?!

228
00:24:11.215 --> 00:24:14.484
Goemon.

229
00:24:14.485 --> 00:24:18.012
You will give me the box.

230
00:24:19.490 --> 00:24:22.824
And what if I say "No"?

231
00:24:28.833 --> 00:24:31.996
You'd do well not to say that.

232
00:24:37.675 --> 00:24:38.375
Sir! Sir!

233
00:24:38.376 --> 00:24:43.748
What's with you.
It's just a joke.

234
00:24:43.749 --> 00:24:48.345
Fine. Here it comes.

235
00:24:51.157 --> 00:24:52.715
Come with me!

236
00:24:59.064 --> 00:25:00.998
See you.

237
00:25:03.035 --> 00:25:04.765
After him.

238
00:25:20.754 --> 00:25:22.688
Hey, that's dangerous!

239
00:26:26.322 --> 00:26:28.415
Alrighty then!

240
00:26:29.425 --> 00:26:32.156
Move, move, move!

241
00:26:39.136 --> 00:26:40.933
Sir!

242
00:28:12.533 --> 00:28:15.934
Seems you haven't
gotten soft yet.

243
00:29:01.151 --> 00:29:02.812
"Through the land"

244
00:29:04.522 --> 00:29:08.958
You're quite determined. Just
what is it with that box?

245
00:29:08.959 --> 00:29:10.860
It's Pandora's Box.

246
00:29:10.861 --> 00:29:13.163
The heck is that?

247
00:29:13.164 --> 00:29:18.467
It's a legend from the
West, a box that,

248
00:29:18.468 --> 00:29:22.598
if opened, will invite calamity.

249
00:29:54.172 --> 00:29:56.333
Do it.

250
00:30:09.087 --> 00:30:10.889
What about the box?

251
00:30:10.890 --> 00:30:17.489
Circumstances have changed.
You've narrowly escaped death.

252
00:30:25.605 --> 00:30:31.169
Sir! Are you all right?!

253
00:30:36.350 --> 00:30:37.908
Delicious!

254
00:30:41.388 --> 00:30:42.955
If you ain't eatin',
I'm takin' it.

255
00:30:42.956 --> 00:30:47.927
Hey! Sir, are we really
bringing this kid along?

256
00:30:47.928 --> 00:30:48.761
Where's the harm?

257
00:30:48.762 --> 00:30:52.632
Harm or no, he'll
just get in the way!

258
00:30:52.633 --> 00:30:58.105
We have a job that requires our
sacred, nay, divine capabilities!

259
00:30:58.106 --> 00:31:01.475
What can this little shit do?

260
00:31:01.476 --> 00:31:06.914
Look, it's not much different
if one burden becomes two.

261
00:31:06.915 --> 00:31:12.920
Yeah, but still...
Hey, that includes me!

262
00:31:12.921 --> 00:31:15.123
Aah, I'm full!

263
00:31:15.124 --> 00:31:17.258
Now then...

264
00:31:17.259 --> 00:31:18.993
What is that? That box.

265
00:31:18.994 --> 00:31:23.064
It's the Pan-something Box.

266
00:31:23.065 --> 00:31:24.999
By the way, sir...

267
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:28.069
Saizo is an
acquaintance of yours?

268
00:31:28.070 --> 00:31:29.070
Why?

269
00:31:29.071 --> 00:31:31.673
I got that feeling somehow.

270
00:31:31.674 --> 00:31:33.074
Well, we're both famous.

271
00:31:33.075 --> 00:31:35.143
Please don't try to fool me.

272
00:31:35.144 --> 00:31:35.777
This bugs you?

273
00:31:35.778 --> 00:31:40.349
This bugs me. You don't tell me
a single thing about your past!

274
00:31:40.350 --> 00:31:41.450
I first had sex at 15.

275
00:31:41.451 --> 00:31:43.752
I'm not asking about that!

276
00:31:43.753 --> 00:31:48.857
I'm just a thief. The greatest thief
in the world, Goemon Ishikawa.

277
00:31:48.858 --> 00:31:50.621
That should be enough.

278
00:31:52.996 --> 00:31:54.496
What are these?

279
00:31:54.497 --> 00:31:55.764
What is it?

280
00:31:55.765 --> 00:31:57.967
It's like a map.

281
00:31:57.968 --> 00:32:02.463
What's with you? You're so loud.
Here.

282
00:32:03.941 --> 00:32:05.542
- Thanks for the food.
- Sir!

283
00:32:05.543 --> 00:32:06.942
Let's go.

284
00:32:14.619 --> 00:32:16.018
Thankya!

285
00:32:18.489 --> 00:32:20.481
The bill.

286
00:32:37.509 --> 00:32:40.211
Here... It's here, right?

287
00:32:40.212 --> 00:32:41.804
Yeah.

288
00:32:46.319 --> 00:32:47.653
This.

289
00:32:47.654 --> 00:32:50.316
It's inside this thing's ear.

290
00:33:17.418 --> 00:33:19.545
I've got something.

291
00:33:21.188 --> 00:33:23.790
Ow! Ow! Ow! I'm stuck!

292
00:33:23.791 --> 00:33:26.427
Ow! Ow! Ow!

293
00:33:26.428 --> 00:33:29.897
Sir! Sir, please help!
Sir, please look!

294
00:33:29.898 --> 00:33:32.299
What's this?

295
00:33:32.300 --> 00:33:36.566
Sir! Sir!

296
00:33:39.974 --> 00:33:42.101
Ow...

297
00:33:50.586 --> 00:33:53.121
A jointly sealed document?

298
00:33:53.122 --> 00:33:58.287
Huh? I think I've seen
these crests somewhere...

299
00:33:59.662 --> 00:34:06.500
Come out. You've followed us all
the way from the restaurant.

300
00:34:11.908 --> 00:34:17.913
Y-Yeah! You've totally been obvious.
Who the hell are you?

301
00:34:17.914 --> 00:34:20.644
Hanzo Hattori.

302
00:34:25.822 --> 00:34:30.526
Um... Hanzo Hattori?!

303
00:34:30.527 --> 00:34:33.520
I'm giving this back.

304
00:34:34.932 --> 00:34:37.167
Who is he?

305
00:34:37.168 --> 00:34:43.707
Everyone knows of him, but no
one has seen him and lived!

306
00:34:43.708 --> 00:34:46.777
He's a legendary shinobi. Shit!

307
00:34:46.778 --> 00:34:48.311
What do you want?

308
00:34:48.312 --> 00:34:51.372
I want to buy that document.

309
00:34:52.650 --> 00:34:55.052
If that's not enough,
I'll get more.

310
00:34:55.053 --> 00:34:57.889
There's no way we'd sell it
for chump change like that!

311
00:34:57.890 --> 00:35:00.525
Fine. I'll sell it.

312
00:35:00.526 --> 00:35:02.493
That's right! Huh?

313
00:35:02.494 --> 00:35:04.894
You're selling it?

314
00:35:09.568 --> 00:35:14.572
If you are out of work,
I know a good employer.

315
00:35:14.573 --> 00:35:18.704
I got no problem gettin' food.

316
00:35:21.414 --> 00:35:23.582
Hey.

317
00:35:23.583 --> 00:35:27.349
Is that thing real?

318
00:35:30.323 --> 00:35:33.192
What was that? Hanzo?!

319
00:35:33.193 --> 00:35:36.895
Possibly at leyasu's command.

320
00:35:36.896 --> 00:35:40.060
That conniving old bastard!

321
00:35:41.502 --> 00:35:45.405
So he knows of the document?

322
00:35:45.406 --> 00:35:49.175
If Goemon gave him the box...

323
00:35:49.176 --> 00:35:55.114
Shit! We finally had our
trump card in hand!

324
00:35:55.115 --> 00:35:58.915
Who the hell is this
"Goemon" anyway?!

325
00:36:00.255 --> 00:36:04.859
My. Such a scary face.

326
00:36:04.860 --> 00:36:12.426
It won't be much longer. If we
can just get that document.

327
00:36:14.202 --> 00:36:17.372
If we have that...

328
00:36:20.408 --> 00:36:26.473
Still, I feel like I've seen
those crests somewhere...

329
00:36:29.051 --> 00:36:31.713
Where was it?

330
00:36:32.989 --> 00:36:36.652
Huh? Huh?

331
00:36:38.561 --> 00:36:42.798
Hey, brat. Have you
seen my short sword?

332
00:36:42.799 --> 00:36:47.069
How would I know about
that stupid thing?

333
00:36:47.070 --> 00:36:49.505
It's not stupid.

334
00:36:49.506 --> 00:36:51.507
Hey, where's Goemon?

335
00:36:51.508 --> 00:36:54.310
Huh? Oh.

336
00:36:54.311 --> 00:36:57.647
He's sleeping, oddly enough.

337
00:36:57.648 --> 00:37:02.779
You hurry and sleep too, brat.
Stupid brat!

338
00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:18.269
Did you get it?

339
00:37:45.197 --> 00:37:47.028
Fall back.

340
00:38:06.820 --> 00:38:10.490
I remember!

341
00:38:10.491 --> 00:38:12.192
What?

342
00:38:12.193 --> 00:38:17.197
Those crests. They're of the
Akechi and Hashiba clans!

343
00:38:17.198 --> 00:38:19.099
The crests on the document!

344
00:38:19.100 --> 00:38:21.668
Akechi? Hashi?

345
00:38:21.669 --> 00:38:27.507
Yes. Akechi as in Mitsuhide Akechi.
The man who, 15 years ago,

346
00:38:27.508 --> 00:38:31.544
betrayed Lord Nobunaga as he
was about to unify Japan,

347
00:38:31.545 --> 00:38:33.447
assassinating him
at Honno Temple.

348
00:38:33.448 --> 00:38:35.116
Who's Hashiba?

349
00:38:35.117 --> 00:38:40.721
Hashiba is Hideyoshi Hashiba, the
former name of Hideyoshi Toyotomi.

350
00:38:40.722 --> 00:38:42.923
It can't be...

351
00:38:42.924 --> 00:38:48.295
So Hideyoshi and Mitsuhide
were secretly aligned.

352
00:38:48.296 --> 00:38:49.864
What does that mean?

353
00:38:49.865 --> 00:38:59.608
It means Lord Hideyoshi himself
planned Nobunaga's assassination.

354
00:38:59.609 --> 00:39:07.983
This document is valuable
proof of that fact.

355
00:39:07.984 --> 00:39:12.087
So, will he act?

356
00:39:12.088 --> 00:39:14.289
Possibly.

357
00:39:14.290 --> 00:39:18.785
Sir! Sir! This isn't
the time for sleeping!

358
00:39:20.230 --> 00:39:23.393
Bastard! Who are you?

359
00:39:31.508 --> 00:39:36.673
Lord Nobunaga's... avenger!

360
00:39:44.655 --> 00:39:47.249
What is the matter?!

361
00:40:10.348 --> 00:40:12.043
Who are you?

362
00:40:33.372 --> 00:40:35.907
Goemon!

363
00:40:35.908 --> 00:40:38.536
Lady Chacha.

364
00:41:09.577 --> 00:41:10.839
Chacha!

365
00:42:30.694 --> 00:42:32.128
Old woman.

366
00:42:32.129 --> 00:42:36.467
Wandering around these parts
at night is dangerous.

367
00:42:36.468 --> 00:42:40.304
They say bandits come out.

368
00:42:40.305 --> 00:42:48.303
Please, sir! The child!
Spare the child! Please!

369
00:42:49.347 --> 00:42:54.513
We got no use for a
wrinkled-up hag like you.

370
00:42:56.355 --> 00:42:58.990
On the other hand...

371
00:42:58.991 --> 00:43:02.560
You're a cute little
thing, aren't you?

372
00:43:02.561 --> 00:43:05.052
I could sell you for plenty.

373
00:43:16.008 --> 00:43:18.477
You little shit!

374
00:44:00.055 --> 00:44:07.621
Boy. Become stronger. Then
nothing can be taken from you.

375
00:44:09.064 --> 00:44:16.266
Will you come with me? I
will make you strong.

376
00:45:09.294 --> 00:45:11.922
Welcome back, Lord Nobunaga.

377
00:45:35.655 --> 00:45:38.356
Lord Nobunaga,
what of the child?

378
00:45:38.357 --> 00:45:41.726
As of today, he is in my care.

379
00:45:41.727 --> 00:45:43.627
Hanzo!

380
00:45:45.031 --> 00:45:47.065
A new shinobi.

381
00:45:47.066 --> 00:45:49.034
His name?

382
00:45:49.035 --> 00:45:51.129
Goemon.

383
00:45:54.741 --> 00:45:57.232
That all right?

384
00:46:26.508 --> 00:46:29.033
Goemon. Saizo.

385
00:46:30.612 --> 00:46:33.946
The winner gets to drink.

386
00:46:40.055 --> 00:46:45.627
The shinobi are shadows.
Shadows have no need for self.

387
00:46:45.628 --> 00:46:51.299
Destroy the self. Be only
a sword for your master.

388
00:46:51.300 --> 00:46:57.439
Never expose yourself. Hide
yourself to the world.

389
00:46:57.440 --> 00:47:02.537
That is the fate of the shinobi.

390
00:47:16.593 --> 00:47:19.791
Enough. Stop.

391
00:47:26.837 --> 00:47:32.104
Those two have
exceptional skill.

392
00:47:35.079 --> 00:47:38.675
So my eyes did not deceive me.

393
00:47:39.818 --> 00:47:41.683
Goemon!

394
00:47:42.854 --> 00:47:44.522
Goemon.

395
00:47:44.523 --> 00:47:47.014
You shouldn't get up yet.

396
00:47:59.671 --> 00:48:01.707
Delish!

397
00:48:01.708 --> 00:48:04.506
Today's newspaper.

398
00:48:06.713 --> 00:48:12.184
Apparently someone murdered
Lord Hideyoshi's double.

399
00:48:12.185 --> 00:48:14.820
On the night you took my
sword and disappeared...

400
00:48:14.821 --> 00:48:17.689
then came back all injured.

401
00:48:17.690 --> 00:48:20.058
Just who are you?

402
00:48:20.059 --> 00:48:21.393
The greatest thief in the...

403
00:48:21.394 --> 00:48:23.563
That's not enough!

404
00:48:23.564 --> 00:48:27.500
A shinobi assigned
directly to Nobunaga Oda.

405
00:48:27.501 --> 00:48:31.037
Now just a thief, huh?

406
00:48:31.038 --> 00:48:33.706
That man brought you here.

407
00:48:33.707 --> 00:48:36.835
Nobody friggin' asked him to.

408
00:48:39.346 --> 00:48:41.644
Mitsunari!

409
00:48:43.584 --> 00:48:45.853
Guarding this castle
is whose job?!

410
00:48:45.854 --> 00:48:48.015
It's my job, sir!

411
00:48:49.891 --> 00:48:52.926
Guarding the castle is left to
you, but your worthlessness

412
00:48:52.927 --> 00:48:56.363
resulted in my
almost being killed!

413
00:48:57.732 --> 00:49:03.737
Do you... want me... to die?

414
00:49:03.738 --> 00:49:06.572
Not at all, sir!

415
00:49:09.712 --> 00:49:12.772
Is that so?

416
00:49:19.522 --> 00:49:24.050
Perhaps... just a
little too bitter.

417
00:49:27.063 --> 00:49:33.867
Ah. That is a most pretty fan.

418
00:49:38.709 --> 00:49:46.449
Were you perhaps visited
by an old acquaintance?

419
00:49:46.450 --> 00:49:47.750
Rikkyu...

420
00:49:47.751 --> 00:49:49.920
Madam?

421
00:49:49.921 --> 00:49:56.622
Rikkyu, why are you in
Lord Hideyoshi's retain?

422
00:49:59.263 --> 00:50:06.737
When I serve tea for great
men, such as Lord Hideyoshi,

423
00:50:06.738 --> 00:50:09.606
I hear a voice.

424
00:50:09.607 --> 00:50:10.640
A voice.

425
00:50:10.641 --> 00:50:17.614
The voice of those
who move the world.

426
00:50:17.615 --> 00:50:25.818
It was Lord Nobunaga
who taught me that.

427
00:50:48.313 --> 00:50:49.347
Goemon!

428
00:50:49.348 --> 00:50:51.182
Sir!

429
00:50:51.183 --> 00:50:54.619
This is my niece, Chacha.

430
00:50:54.620 --> 00:50:58.957
As of today, she is staying
here in the castle.

431
00:50:58.958 --> 00:51:01.222
You will protect her.

432
00:51:32.860 --> 00:51:38.198
Father... Mother...

433
00:51:38.199 --> 00:51:40.734
Don't go.

434
00:51:40.735 --> 00:51:43.397
Father!

435
00:52:34.391 --> 00:52:39.228
Goemon... Goemon!

436
00:52:39.229 --> 00:52:41.464
I'm here.

437
00:52:41.465 --> 00:52:44.133
I had a scary dream.

438
00:52:44.134 --> 00:52:49.732
I am here. Please rest easy.

439
00:52:50.975 --> 00:52:52.242
Goemon?

440
00:52:52.243 --> 00:52:54.478
Yes.

441
00:52:54.479 --> 00:52:59.149
Where are your
father and mother?

442
00:52:59.150 --> 00:53:01.485
I have none.

443
00:53:01.486 --> 00:53:05.856
Oh. Then we're the same.

444
00:53:05.857 --> 00:53:17.769
My father died in battle. Even now...
I dream of that time.

445
00:53:17.770 --> 00:53:20.534
Over and over again.

446
00:53:22.308 --> 00:53:24.642
And friends?

447
00:53:24.643 --> 00:53:28.179
Do you have friends?

448
00:53:28.180 --> 00:53:32.140
Yes. Just one.

449
00:53:32.953 --> 00:53:36.021
What's his name?

450
00:53:36.022 --> 00:53:39.024
His name is Saizo.

451
00:53:39.025 --> 00:53:47.023
I hope I can make
friends someday, too.

452
00:54:27.542 --> 00:54:31.345
I thought you would be bored,
always being inside the castle.

453
00:54:31.346 --> 00:54:36.580
But it would not be good if
Lord Nobunaga learned of this.

454
00:54:43.760 --> 00:54:45.060
Goemon?

455
00:54:45.061 --> 00:54:46.790
Yes.

456
00:54:50.433 --> 00:54:55.804
Do you think we've
become friends?

457
00:54:56.774 --> 00:55:02.974
Thanks to you, I no
longer have scary dreams.

458
00:55:18.963 --> 00:55:20.954
Here.

459
00:55:28.940 --> 00:55:31.670
Thank you for everything.

460
00:55:43.022 --> 00:55:45.149
Goodbye.

461
00:56:12.352 --> 00:56:14.353
Goemon.

462
00:56:14.354 --> 00:56:16.049
I am here.

463
00:56:24.031 --> 00:56:26.465
As thanks for Chacha.

464
00:56:43.084 --> 00:56:46.350
Have you gotten stronger?

465
00:56:49.591 --> 00:56:54.255
I... still don't know.

466
00:56:55.264 --> 00:56:58.597
That's good enough.

467
00:57:07.410 --> 00:57:10.112
What's that? Lord Nobunaga?!

468
00:57:10.113 --> 00:57:15.176
Mitsuhide Akechi rebelled.
At Honno Temple.

469
00:57:23.560 --> 00:57:26.393
So it's done.

470
00:57:37.441 --> 00:57:46.941
Good work. Sorry, but I will
take control of everything.

471
00:58:00.165 --> 00:58:03.999
Lord Nobunaga!

472
00:58:16.415 --> 00:58:21.753
Mitsunari Ishida?
Become his underlings?

473
00:58:21.754 --> 00:58:27.459
Lords Hideyoshi and Mitsunari
were both born poor farmers.

474
00:58:27.460 --> 00:58:34.132
But they came this far, high
enough to control everything.

475
00:58:34.133 --> 00:58:41.941
So some day, even we should
be able to become samurai.

476
00:58:41.942 --> 00:58:45.211
I'm fine.

477
00:58:45.212 --> 00:58:50.946
I want to try being free.

478
00:58:57.859 --> 00:59:00.157
A farewell gift.

479
00:59:11.205 --> 00:59:14.241
"Through the land"

480
00:59:14.242 --> 00:59:16.301
"Spread militarism"

481
00:59:29.224 --> 00:59:31.159
What became of your sword?

482
00:59:31.160 --> 00:59:33.390
I threw it away.

483
00:59:35.064 --> 00:59:39.100
I won't say "Thank you."

484
00:59:39.101 --> 00:59:45.708
I don't need it. It would be
unpleasant coming from you.

485
00:59:45.709 --> 00:59:48.277
If Hideyoshi were simply killed,

486
00:59:48.278 --> 00:59:51.714
the world would go back
to fighting and chaos.

487
00:59:51.715 --> 00:59:56.919
Wars would erupt and many
innocent civilians would die.

488
00:59:56.920 --> 01:00:02.292
So what? I'm free
to do what I like.

489
01:00:02.293 --> 01:00:08.061
If you hadn't stolen the box, that
boy's mother wouldn't have died.

490
01:00:10.301 --> 01:00:16.206
If you enjoy your freedom,
stop getting others involved.

491
01:00:18.376 --> 01:00:21.411
Simply living without
purpose isn't being free.

492
01:00:21.412 --> 01:00:23.113
You know that, don't you?

493
01:00:23.114 --> 01:00:28.052
And what about you?! The henchman
for an idiot boss, worked hard

494
01:00:28.053 --> 01:00:30.385
and hands stained with blood.

495
01:00:31.823 --> 01:00:34.558
Just a little more...

496
01:00:34.559 --> 01:00:41.065
Just a little more, and I can
become a samurai. And then...

497
01:00:41.066 --> 01:00:46.637
Sheeit. This got wet.

498
01:00:46.638 --> 01:00:51.275
For an unpopular guy,
you give long sermons.

499
01:00:51.276 --> 01:00:54.445
I have a wife and child.

500
01:00:54.446 --> 01:00:57.348
I feel bad for your wife.

501
01:00:57.349 --> 01:00:59.078
Indeed...

502
01:01:02.921 --> 01:01:09.691
I doubt we'll meet again.
If we do...

503
01:01:13.466 --> 01:01:15.593
I'll kill you.

504
01:01:20.339 --> 01:01:21.328
Hey.

505
01:01:25.178 --> 01:01:30.708
That clothing really suits you.
You should change jobs.

506
01:01:34.555 --> 01:01:40.693
You're way too flashy.
Being a thief...

507
01:01:40.694 --> 01:01:43.185
The greatest thief.

508
01:01:44.198 --> 01:01:47.395
Don't toot your own horn.

509
01:01:52.740 --> 01:01:58.545
Rikkyu... Is it true
that war will begin?

510
01:01:58.546 --> 01:02:00.581
Why would you say that?

511
01:02:00.582 --> 01:02:06.553
I hear them, too. The voices.

512
01:02:06.554 --> 01:02:11.925
Not war... No matter
what, war must not...

513
01:02:11.926 --> 01:02:17.765
I understand. That is
why this current plan

514
01:02:17.766 --> 01:02:23.338
must be prevented at all costs.

515
01:02:23.339 --> 01:02:25.707
It is far too reckless.

516
01:02:25.708 --> 01:02:27.842
Then Lord Hideyoshi and I...

517
01:02:27.843 --> 01:02:34.382
No! If you do that, you would
consent to Lord Hideyoshi

518
01:02:34.383 --> 01:02:37.753
and become his concubine.

519
01:02:37.754 --> 01:02:44.026
Please leave this to me.
After all,

520
01:02:44.027 --> 01:02:48.964
tea cannot be served if
the world is in turmoil.

521
01:02:48.965 --> 01:02:54.232
In which case, I would
have nothing to do.

522
01:03:13.591 --> 01:03:17.288
Look. Yes, that's it. It spun!

523
01:03:23.769 --> 01:03:31.403
Everyone, thank you for gathering.
There's something I want you to see.

524
01:03:44.324 --> 01:03:49.695
I do not care for the Christians. But
while they call their work "missions,"

525
01:03:49.696 --> 01:03:55.767
the weapons they secretly
possess are outstanding.

526
01:03:55.768 --> 01:04:01.873
This was an expensive purchase. I
want to mass produce these at once,

527
01:04:01.874 --> 01:04:06.778
and attack Korea and China!

528
01:04:12.620 --> 01:04:15.953
I will show you something else.

529
01:04:38.046 --> 01:04:45.920
You should have just...
stuck to serving tea.

530
01:04:51.827 --> 01:05:00.257
He found fault with my dream...

531
01:05:03.739 --> 01:05:05.507
I will send my soldiers!

532
01:05:05.508 --> 01:05:08.000
No, I will!

533
01:05:10.080 --> 01:05:13.015
Kato, give soldiers.
Onishi, give supplies.

534
01:05:13.016 --> 01:05:15.051
And I, sir?

535
01:05:15.052 --> 01:05:21.590
Mitsunari? I didn't
notice you there.

536
01:05:21.591 --> 01:05:29.327
Now then, everyone... It's war!

537
01:05:30.702 --> 01:05:34.229
The boss sure is a slave driver.

538
01:05:35.440 --> 01:05:37.074
Sasuke, you want to
be an official, too?

539
01:05:37.075 --> 01:05:37.941
Huh?

540
01:05:37.942 --> 01:05:39.943
An official. You want to
be someone important?

541
01:05:39.944 --> 01:05:42.312
Well, of course! Listen,

542
01:05:42.313 --> 01:05:47.250
people like us aren't suited
for commerce or rice planting.

543
01:05:47.251 --> 01:05:52.457
But as long as we're not officials,
that's all we'll ever have. Ever!

544
01:05:52.458 --> 01:05:56.928
So anyone would jump at the chance.
Let's see...

545
01:05:56.929 --> 01:06:00.131
Yukimura Sanada's employ
would be pretty good, huh?

546
01:06:00.132 --> 01:06:04.068
Then I'd buy a mansion, get
some girls, find a bride...

547
01:06:04.069 --> 01:06:09.974
Or maybe get the bride first!
Ah, you ain't even listening.

548
01:06:11.009 --> 01:06:13.244
Koheita.

549
01:06:13.245 --> 01:06:15.237
Hey, what is it?

550
01:06:21.087 --> 01:06:23.578
Idiot! Don't!

551
01:06:27.026 --> 01:06:29.328
Rikkyu is?

552
01:06:29.329 --> 01:06:33.527
His death is a great loss.

553
01:06:41.175 --> 01:06:45.339
There is something I
wish to show you.

554
01:07:01.963 --> 01:07:06.059
I'm back. Open up.

555
01:07:09.037 --> 01:07:12.234
What is it, Okichi?

556
01:07:16.244 --> 01:07:23.151
I... will kill Hideyoshi.

557
01:07:23.152 --> 01:07:30.826
If that... if that
will stop this war.

558
01:07:30.827 --> 01:07:34.563
You're truly fine with this?

559
01:07:34.564 --> 01:07:42.028
Yes. However, I
have one request.

560
01:07:45.676 --> 01:07:49.373
Sasuke sure is takin' his time.

561
01:07:53.450 --> 01:07:56.510
Getting drunk?

562
01:07:57.921 --> 01:08:01.948
Took you a long time to notice.

563
01:08:07.065 --> 01:08:11.201
This isn't a place to
come to with another guy.

564
01:08:11.202 --> 01:08:13.762
Indeed.

565
01:08:21.079 --> 01:08:27.585
That is... far too reckless.
Please reconsider.

566
01:08:27.586 --> 01:08:28.553
Shut up!

567
01:08:28.554 --> 01:08:30.421
But...

568
01:08:30.422 --> 01:08:34.726
I'll give you 200.

569
01:08:34.727 --> 01:08:39.063
That's right. You'll
have your own salary.

570
01:08:39.064 --> 01:08:42.634
With that, you can join
the ranks of the samurai.

571
01:08:42.635 --> 01:08:47.306
That's what you want, isn't it?
No?

572
01:08:47.307 --> 01:08:53.479
This is the only way.
The only one.

573
01:08:53.480 --> 01:08:59.282
So you weren't harmed? I'm glad.

574
01:09:06.526 --> 01:09:08.084
Here.

575
01:09:18.172 --> 01:09:23.877
How many years has it
been since we came here?

576
01:09:23.878 --> 01:09:27.678
Nothing has changed, has it?

577
01:09:31.186 --> 01:09:33.677
Lady Chacha...

578
01:09:36.191 --> 01:09:37.058
I...

579
01:09:37.059 --> 01:09:44.565
Goodbye. I came to
tell you goodbye.

580
01:09:44.566 --> 01:09:51.699
Lady Chacha will officially become
Lord Hideyoshi's concubine.

581
01:09:55.878 --> 01:09:58.574
Take care of yourself.

582
01:10:00.650 --> 01:10:04.853
In three days, a celebration will
be held on Lord Hideyoshi's boat

583
01:10:04.854 --> 01:10:09.057
for the dispatching
of the troops.

584
01:10:09.058 --> 01:10:16.099
That will be Lady Chacha's
introduction as his concubine.

585
01:10:16.100 --> 01:10:23.404
Ieyasu Tokugawa...
What are you after?

586
01:10:57.910 --> 01:10:59.969
"Through the land"

587
01:11:01.247 --> 01:11:03.408
"Spread militarism"

588
01:11:15.260 --> 01:11:20.131
My song will be the signal.

589
01:11:20.132 --> 01:11:23.761
Avenge Lord Nobunaga!

590
01:11:24.570 --> 01:11:32.306
That is the only way
to save Lady Chacha.

591
01:11:42.923 --> 01:11:47.360
Sir. You've been out late.

592
01:11:49.496 --> 01:11:51.464
What happened?

593
01:11:51.465 --> 01:11:54.467
Son of a bitch!

594
01:11:54.468 --> 01:11:54.501
Hey! Hey!

595
01:11:54.502 --> 01:11:56.535
That's what happened.

596
01:11:56.536 --> 01:12:00.632
So did he die?

597
01:12:05.046 --> 01:12:08.181
I became stronger.

598
01:12:08.182 --> 01:12:15.489
I became strong and I killed him.
I frickin' killed him!

599
01:12:15.490 --> 01:12:17.324
Sir!

600
01:12:17.325 --> 01:12:19.359
Sir! Please stop.

601
01:12:19.360 --> 01:12:21.194
Get over there!

602
01:12:21.195 --> 01:12:24.631
Hey!

603
01:12:24.632 --> 01:12:29.737
Listen. This ain't what
your mother wanted!

604
01:12:29.738 --> 01:12:37.378
Would your mom say to avenge her?
To kill someone?

605
01:12:37.379 --> 01:12:41.315
She wouldn't want revenge!

606
01:13:34.940 --> 01:13:39.743
What do you think? A
spectacle, isn't it? Look.

607
01:13:39.744 --> 01:13:48.584
Look how many men have assembled.
For me and for you.

608
01:13:51.556 --> 01:13:53.558
Excuse me.

609
01:13:53.559 --> 01:13:57.128
Good work, everyone.
Does anyone need water?

610
01:13:57.129 --> 01:13:59.464
Does anyone need water?

611
01:13:59.465 --> 01:14:05.904
Won't anyone sing? Well?

612
01:14:05.905 --> 01:14:08.999
You're no fun.

613
01:14:10.676 --> 01:14:12.577
I shall.

614
01:14:12.578 --> 01:14:17.607
Ah, Lord Tokugawa. Very well.

615
01:14:23.190 --> 01:14:34.300
♪ To think that a man
has but 50 years... ♪

616
01:14:34.301 --> 01:14:39.006
That's right. Kill him.

617
01:14:39.007 --> 01:14:46.313
Do it in front of everyone. News of
Hideyoshi's death will go public,

618
01:14:46.314 --> 01:14:50.017
and the world will again
be plunged into war.

619
01:14:50.018 --> 01:14:55.322
If we take advantage of that chaos,
the one closest to taking control...

620
01:14:55.323 --> 01:14:56.813
will be you.

621
01:15:00.562 --> 01:15:08.833
♪ ... a vain dream...  ♪

622
01:15:13.509 --> 01:15:16.034
Give me your fan.

623
01:15:21.751 --> 01:15:27.990
♪ To think that a man
has but 50 years... ♪

624
01:15:27.991 --> 01:15:36.031
♪ To think that a man has but ♪ ♪
50 years to live under heaven... ♪

625
01:15:36.032 --> 01:15:41.603
One day, I will put an
end to the fighting.

626
01:15:41.604 --> 01:15:46.009
I will create a world
without fighting!

627
01:15:46.010 --> 01:15:49.741
I dance for that day...

628
01:15:51.949 --> 01:15:54.679
Don't let others call the steps!

629
01:15:57.555 --> 01:15:58.954
Dance!

630
01:16:00.391 --> 01:16:05.296
"She wouldn't want
revenge," huh?

631
01:16:05.297 --> 01:16:09.256
I said those words.

632
01:16:46.672 --> 01:16:48.664
What's happening?!

633
01:17:00.988 --> 01:17:02.182
This way!

634
01:19:20.968 --> 01:19:23.596
Good work.

635
01:20:46.323 --> 01:20:47.551
Come on!

636
01:21:07.278 --> 01:21:11.010
I'm alive!

637
01:21:14.787 --> 01:21:17.889
I can't go.

638
01:21:17.890 --> 01:21:20.290
Please go, Goemon.

639
01:21:24.697 --> 01:21:30.761
That shinobi... is still alive.

640
01:21:33.940 --> 01:21:36.204
Please go.

641
01:21:37.410 --> 01:21:39.469
Please go!

642
01:21:44.817 --> 01:21:54.489
Wait! Don't kill him. Make him say...
who hired him.

643
01:21:58.665 --> 01:22:01.734
Say nothing if you value
your family's lives.

644
01:22:01.735 --> 01:22:04.602
How dare you attack
Lord Hideyoshi?!

645
01:22:24.825 --> 01:22:26.593
Do you know?

646
01:22:26.594 --> 01:22:29.461
Apparently, he's at Sonezaki.

647
01:22:31.599 --> 01:22:37.605
Sir, please don't. Saizo surely
prepared himself for this.

648
01:22:37.606 --> 01:22:40.803
What's your name? Huh?

649
01:22:44.513 --> 01:22:46.113
Speak!

650
01:22:46.114 --> 01:22:51.719
If you help him... things
will get very difficult.

651
01:22:51.720 --> 01:22:54.848
Just think of it as fate.

652
01:22:59.529 --> 01:23:03.231
Do you really get it?!

653
01:23:03.232 --> 01:23:04.824
Yeah.

654
01:23:17.346 --> 01:23:19.541
I get it.

655
01:23:29.726 --> 01:23:32.524
We meet again.

656
01:23:36.366 --> 01:23:38.596
Don't kill me.

657
01:23:40.571 --> 01:23:48.946
What? He escaped? You
will get him back!

658
01:23:48.947 --> 01:23:55.409
I believe you already know, but...
bring him alive.

659
01:24:11.303 --> 01:24:12.637
Sir! This is bad!

660
01:24:12.638 --> 01:24:13.771
What is it? They found us here?

661
01:24:13.772 --> 01:24:15.373
No!

662
01:24:15.374 --> 01:24:17.968
They're going after...

663
01:24:20.546 --> 01:24:22.946
Saizo's family!

664
01:24:49.777 --> 01:24:51.811
What is it?

665
01:24:51.812 --> 01:24:58.308
I told you! I said things
would get difficult!

666
01:25:06.427 --> 01:25:09.794
Okichi! Okichi!

667
01:26:12.496 --> 01:26:14.589
Saizo!

668
01:26:18.737 --> 01:26:23.741
Look! This is the
freedom you spoke of!

669
01:26:23.742 --> 01:26:27.075
This is the price to
pay for your freedom!

670
01:27:13.627 --> 01:27:18.792
"Come to the castle if you
value your child's life."

671
01:27:24.005 --> 01:27:27.304
Please move. Please move!

672
01:27:52.367 --> 01:27:57.038
Well? Just tell me your name.

673
01:27:57.039 --> 01:28:01.509
Do that, and at least your
child's life will be spared.

674
01:28:01.510 --> 01:28:02.944
Hey!

675
01:28:02.945 --> 01:28:04.479
Saizo!

676
01:28:04.480 --> 01:28:05.347
Please move.

677
01:28:05.348 --> 01:28:08.283
Hey! Hey!

678
01:28:42.920 --> 01:28:46.990
My name is...

679
01:28:46.991 --> 01:28:52.555
My name is... Goemon!

680
01:28:55.500 --> 01:28:58.335
That's Goemon?

681
01:28:58.336 --> 01:29:03.407
That's right! I am...

682
01:29:03.408 --> 01:29:09.180
the world's greatest
thief, Goemon Ishikawa!

683
01:29:09.181 --> 01:29:10.181
Stop it!

684
01:29:10.182 --> 01:29:16.288
I've done so many bad things.
I've had a fun, interesting life.

685
01:29:16.289 --> 01:29:21.259
I thought I'd kill Lord Hideyoshi
and go down in history,

686
01:29:21.260 --> 01:29:23.595
but that's luck for you.

687
01:29:23.596 --> 01:29:27.432
I'm Goemon! I'm Goemon Ishikawa!

688
01:29:27.433 --> 01:29:28.266
Still...

689
01:29:28.267 --> 01:29:29.968
Move!

690
01:29:29.969 --> 01:29:34.040
How nice of you all
to gather here.

691
01:29:34.041 --> 01:29:37.875
Now that's a sight!

692
01:29:39.479 --> 01:29:41.781
You all!

693
01:29:41.782 --> 01:29:50.056
You wondering why I tried to snuff
Lord Hideyoshi? You want to know?

694
01:29:50.057 --> 01:29:55.662
Just look at this world!
Isn't it insane?!

695
01:29:55.663 --> 01:29:59.733
Time after time, guys appear
seeking absolute power,

696
01:29:59.734 --> 01:30:06.907
killing each other, spilling blood.
And they all say the same thing:

697
01:30:06.908 --> 01:30:10.410
"This is the last time."

698
01:30:10.411 --> 01:30:17.284
But that promise hasn't been
kept once, has it? Well?!

699
01:30:18.821 --> 01:30:20.154
Stop it, Saizo.

700
01:30:20.155 --> 01:30:25.126
And whose blood
gets spilled first?

701
01:30:25.127 --> 01:30:28.494
It's your blood, isn't it?!

702
01:30:30.866 --> 01:30:33.368
That's enough! Saizo!

703
01:30:33.369 --> 01:30:36.938
Everyone, remember
this sight forever!

704
01:30:36.939 --> 01:30:38.507
Stop it!

705
01:30:38.508 --> 01:30:43.343
This is Goemon Ishikawa's
final performance!

706
01:31:16.714 --> 01:31:19.706
You're lonely by yourself, huh?

707
01:32:26.152 --> 01:32:33.719
How many times did I tell you?
"Stop it"?

708
01:32:34.828 --> 01:32:39.595
How many times did I tell you
things would get difficult?!

709
01:32:41.769 --> 01:32:47.332
I can't stay with you anymore.

710
01:33:44.868 --> 01:33:47.470
Mitsunari.

711
01:33:47.471 --> 01:33:48.838
Sir.

712
01:33:48.839 --> 01:33:57.814
That shinobi earlier... he
told me his name was "Saizo."

713
01:33:57.815 --> 01:34:00.409
That's your shinobi, isn't it?

714
01:34:03.421 --> 01:34:07.380
Hey! What the hell
are you doing?

715
01:34:08.826 --> 01:34:15.595
There must be some mistake. I
did not know that individual.

716
01:34:19.104 --> 01:34:20.833
"Spread militarism"

717
01:34:25.511 --> 01:34:29.174
Has Goemon arrived?

718
01:36:03.446 --> 01:36:06.282
Don't take all the
glory for yourself.

719
01:36:06.283 --> 01:36:10.686
You are not the only
one who mourns Saizo.

720
01:36:10.687 --> 01:36:14.890
Let us handle this.
You go on ahead.

721
01:36:14.891 --> 01:36:17.660
Fine.

722
01:36:17.661 --> 01:36:19.822
Just don't die.

723
01:37:30.203 --> 01:37:33.901
So you've made
your move, Goemon.

724
01:37:35.476 --> 01:37:43.247
Now then, shall he or Lady
Chacha strike Hideyoshi first?

725
01:40:19.313 --> 01:40:24.217
I thought you agreed to be
my concubine quite suddenly.

726
01:40:24.218 --> 01:40:26.486
This is why?

727
01:40:26.487 --> 01:40:29.980
For what you did
to Lord Nobunaga!

728
01:40:35.264 --> 01:40:41.669
Yeah... I've gotta settle
things with you, huh?

729
01:40:44.673 --> 01:40:46.971
The same trick won't work twice.

730
01:40:54.450 --> 01:41:00.322
I see. So that document
still remained?

731
01:41:00.323 --> 01:41:06.962
Mitsuhide Akechi was no fool.
However...

732
01:41:06.963 --> 01:41:11.667
If you kill me, then what?

733
01:41:11.668 --> 01:41:17.505
You want to return us
to a time of strife?

734
01:41:22.379 --> 01:41:26.549
The war will not end.

735
01:41:26.550 --> 01:41:32.853
No matter how much time
passes, nothing will change.

736
01:42:33.954 --> 01:42:39.926
So you're finally here.
It's been a long time.

737
01:42:39.927 --> 01:42:44.764
Sorry to keep you waiting.

738
01:42:44.765 --> 01:42:48.868
I've come to take you to hell.

739
01:42:48.869 --> 01:42:54.774
Well, before that...
how about a drink?

740
01:43:04.218 --> 01:43:07.421
A nice view, isn't it?

741
01:43:07.422 --> 01:43:13.827
It is. That's why I
built this here.

742
01:43:15.063 --> 01:43:22.102
What did it feel like?
Controlling everything.

743
01:43:22.103 --> 01:43:29.670
It was quite good. Not as
good as this sake, though.

744
01:43:32.347 --> 01:43:37.585
Why did you kill Lord Nobunaga?

745
01:43:37.586 --> 01:43:41.589
You were his top subordinate.

746
01:43:41.590 --> 01:43:44.992
I was hungry.

747
01:43:47.130 --> 01:43:53.635
As you know, I was
born a poor farmer.

748
01:43:53.636 --> 01:44:02.044
Since I was a child, I've been
so hungry that I can't stand it.

749
01:44:02.045 --> 01:44:08.318
Just once, I wanted
to feel full.

750
01:44:08.319 --> 01:44:14.724
That's why I strove to meet
Nobunaga's unreasonable demands,

751
01:44:14.725 --> 01:44:18.461
working and moving upward.

752
01:44:18.462 --> 01:44:26.970
But no matter how much I
ate, it wasn't enough.

753
01:44:26.971 --> 01:44:35.813
No matter how much time passed,
I stayed hungry. Famished.

754
01:44:35.814 --> 01:44:46.757
So, finally, I wanted to
try eating everything.

755
01:44:46.758 --> 01:44:50.923
That's all there is to it.

756
01:44:53.232 --> 01:44:57.692
Have any last words?

757
01:45:06.846 --> 01:45:13.219
How did it feel, to be free?

758
01:45:13.220 --> 01:45:28.768
You fled 15 years ago. To be free,
you fled from your own destiny.

759
01:45:28.769 --> 01:45:35.542
So, did you find it?

760
01:45:35.543 --> 01:45:39.570
Did you become free?

761
01:45:42.150 --> 01:45:47.452
Go on. Do it.

762
01:45:49.457 --> 01:45:57.229
You can't flee anymore.
Not from your destiny.

763
01:47:11.410 --> 01:47:15.646
So Mitsunari has already
raised the troops?

764
01:47:15.647 --> 01:47:18.416
Is it war?

765
01:47:18.417 --> 01:47:27.486
No. Just a competition. For
the bait called "power."

766
01:47:36.836 --> 01:47:39.338
We possess authority!

767
01:47:39.339 --> 01:47:43.208
This document proves
that leyasu Tokugawa

768
01:47:43.209 --> 01:47:47.747
is the rightful successor
to Lord Nobunaga!

769
01:47:47.748 --> 01:47:53.286
With Hideyoshi Toyotomi dead,
who else but Lord leyasu

770
01:47:53.287 --> 01:47:58.691
must restore order
to the world?!

771
01:48:13.942 --> 01:48:17.207
I leave the rest to you.

772
01:49:08.865 --> 01:49:12.164
Is it to avenge a friend?

773
01:49:14.205 --> 01:49:17.834
Loyalty to a benefactor?

774
01:49:22.046 --> 01:49:26.346
They wouldn't want that.

775
01:49:48.807 --> 01:49:51.401
Take this.

776
01:49:52.978 --> 01:49:59.714
Please... Please be
sure to come back.

777
01:50:32.186 --> 01:50:34.053
Move out!

778
01:50:34.054 --> 01:50:35.749
Drive them back.

779
01:50:48.637 --> 01:50:50.471
That's a terrible thing
you've got there.

780
01:50:50.472 --> 01:50:52.206
I'm going, too!

781
01:50:52.207 --> 01:50:53.908
Say...

782
01:50:53.909 --> 01:50:58.212
Do you know this story?

783
01:50:58.213 --> 01:51:02.951
A girl gets curious and opens a
box that shouldn't be opened.

784
01:51:02.952 --> 01:51:05.153
What are you talking about?

785
01:51:05.154 --> 01:51:08.823
All kinds of disasters
are inside that box.

786
01:51:08.824 --> 01:51:14.629
Disease, war, hatred... they come
flying out, plaguing people.

787
01:51:14.630 --> 01:51:18.567
But the girl didn't let
one last thing out.

788
01:51:18.568 --> 01:51:24.574
Thanks to that, humanity wasn't wiped out.
Do you know what it was?

789
01:51:24.575 --> 01:51:27.243
What was it?

790
01:51:27.244 --> 01:51:30.645
Something I'd lost.

791
01:51:55.707 --> 01:51:58.767
Become strong, Koheita.

792
01:52:00.378 --> 01:52:03.006
A lot stronger than me.

793
01:53:11.718 --> 01:53:13.710
Lord Nobunaga?

794
01:53:52.961 --> 01:53:54.895
I bring news! Lord Nobunaga...

795
01:53:54.896 --> 01:54:00.267
Lord Nobunaga has
joined the fighting!

796
01:54:01.237 --> 01:54:04.434
What idiocy is this?

797
01:56:14.209 --> 01:56:16.268
Make no moves!

798
01:56:24.119 --> 01:56:26.417
Have you gone mad?

799
01:56:28.156 --> 01:56:30.421
Move aside!

800
01:57:01.692 --> 01:57:04.923
If it weren't for you all...

801
01:57:07.698 --> 01:57:11.657
This never ends because
you're fighting for power!

802
01:57:13.470 --> 01:57:17.498
No one can be happy!

803
01:57:20.845 --> 01:57:29.048
We are fighting for
that happiness as well!

804
01:57:36.495 --> 01:57:41.364
I'm tired of hearing
things like that!

805
01:58:54.309 --> 01:58:57.073
Ieyasu...

806
01:59:00.482 --> 01:59:04.442
Swear that this is the end!

807
01:59:08.658 --> 01:59:12.754
Swear that this will
end the fighting!

808
01:59:17.133 --> 01:59:21.832
Swear that everyone can
live in happiness!

809
01:59:33.017 --> 01:59:34.985
Goemon!

810
01:59:43.160 --> 01:59:50.134
I got the man who tried to
strike down Lord leyasu!

811
01:59:50.135 --> 01:59:56.768
I did it! It was my doing!

812
01:59:58.143 --> 02:00:02.842
I did it! By my hands!

813
02:00:05.050 --> 02:00:10.622
Hey! I did it! Hey!

814
02:00:10.623 --> 02:00:13.888
Where's my reward?

815
02:00:15.728 --> 02:00:19.186
Where's my reward?!

816
02:00:24.137 --> 02:00:28.198
Tears from heaven, eh?

817
02:00:29.842 --> 02:00:33.574
We must finish this.

818
02:01:44.421 --> 02:01:50.291
Now that's a sight...
